# SPDX-License-Identifier: MPL-2.0
# The labels of a structural plan keep off the members that cross a beam.
# A bay of 6 by 12 m: four columns, two rafters along y and three purlins
# along x, the middle purlin crossing the rafters at their middles. On
# paper at 1:100 each rafter's label moves along it off the middle purlin,
# a purlin between two rafters keeps its middle, and each column has its
# type beside it. An ordinary floor plan labels none of them.
import ui/panels/bim_plan_panel.dl

# `amount` to tenths, as "18.7".
function the label test text of {a 64 bit floating-point number:amount}:
    execute:
        set tenths to (the floor of (((the absolute value of amount) * 10.0) + 0.5)) as a 64 bit integer
        set sign to the string form of ""
        if (amount < 0.0) and (tenths > (0 as a 64 bit integer)):
            set sign to the string form of "-"
        return ((sign + (the string form of (tenths / (10 as a 64 bit integer)))) + (the string form of ".")) + (the string form of (the remainder of tenths divided by (10 as a 64 bit integer)))

function show label test labels of {bim canvas record:canvas} titled {a string:title}:
    execute:
        print ((title + (the string form of ": ")) + (the string form of (the length of (canvas's texts's values)))) as a line
        loop cursor from 0 to the length of (canvas's texts's values):
            set shownLabel to the item at cursor in (canvas's texts's values)
            print ((((the string form of "  ") + shownLabel's message) + (the string form of " at ")) + (((the label test text of shownLabel's anchor's x) + (the string form of ", ")) + (the label test text of shownLabel's anchor's y))) as a line

set editor to a new bim editor
set e to the address of editor
set target to the address of (editor's documentValue's current)
set postType to add bim linear type named (the string form of "HEA 200") as role bim column role sized 0.2 by 0.19 round false of (the string form of "steel") to target
set rafterType to add bim linear type named (the string form of "IPE 330") as role bim beam role sized 0.16 by 0.33 round false of (the string form of "steel") to target
set purlinType to add bim linear type named (the string form of "IPE 160") as role bim beam role sized 0.082 by 0.16 round false of (the string form of "steel") to target
loop bay from 0 to 2:
    set bayX to (bay as a 64 bit floating-point number) * 6.0
    ignore add bim linear typed postType on editor's levelId from (a cad vector3 with x bayX, y 0.0 and z 0.0) to (a cad vector3 with x bayX, y 0.0 and z 6.0) turned 0.0 to target
    ignore add bim linear typed postType on editor's levelId from (a cad vector3 with x bayX, y 12.0 and z 0.0) to (a cad vector3 with x bayX, y 12.0 and z 6.0) turned 0.0 to target
    ignore add bim linear typed rafterType on editor's levelId from (a cad vector3 with x bayX, y 0.0 and z 6.0) to (a cad vector3 with x bayX, y 12.0 and z 6.0) turned 0.0 to target
loop row from 0 to 3:
    set rowY to (row as a 64 bit floating-point number) * 6.0
    ignore add bim linear typed purlinType on editor's levelId from (a cad vector3 with x 0.0, y rowY and z 6.2) to (a cad vector3 with x 6.0, y rowY and z 6.2) turned 0.0 to target

set paperTransform to @intrinsic("construct", a bim drawing transform record, (a cad vector2 with x 0.0 and y 0.0), (a cad vector2 with x 0.0 and y 0.0), 10.0)
set plainCanvas to a new bim canvas
set plainCanvas's paperScale to 1.0
draw bim annotations in plan of editor through paperTransform on (the address of plainCanvas)
show label test labels of plainCanvas titled (the string form of "floor plan")

type bim editor key 2117 in e
print editor's message as a line
set paperCanvas to a new bim canvas
set paperCanvas's paperScale to 1.0
draw bim annotations in plan of editor through paperTransform on (the address of paperCanvas)
show label test labels of paperCanvas titled (the string form of "structural plan at 1:100 (mm)")
